	"NavMega",
	"NavMorph",
	"import Preview from \"@components/_docs/Preview.astro\";\nimport PropsTable from \"@components/_docs/PropsTable.astro\";\nimport AnnouncementBanner from \"@components/AnnouncementBanner.astro\";\n\nSite-wide announcement banner. Optionally a link, optionally dismissible, hides on scroll-down and reappears on scroll-up. Content and scheduling live in the `announcements` content collection — editors publish, queue, or expire banners by editing markdown files, no code changes.\n\n## Preview\n\n<Preview label=\"Plain — no link, dismissible\">\n  <div class=\"relative w-full\">\n    <AnnouncementBanner class=\"bg-intent text-fg-on-intent\">\n      <span><strong>New:</strong> Component showcase is live</span>\n    </AnnouncementBanner>\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n<Preview label=\"As a link with arrow\">\n  <div class=\"relative w-full\">\n    <AnnouncementBanner href=\"/series-a\" class=\"bg-intent text-fg-on-intent\" dismissible={false}>\n      <span><strong>Read the post:</strong> Announcing our Series A</span>\n    </AnnouncementBanner>\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n## Props\n\n<PropsTable props={[\n  { name: \"href\", type: \"string\", description: \"When set, the banner becomes a clickable link with a trailing arrow icon.\" },\n  { name: \"dismissible\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"true\", description: \"Show a close button that dismisses for the session.\" },\n  { name: \"class\", type: \"string\", description: \"Additional classes — typically background + text color (e.g. bg-intent text-fg-on-intent).\" },\n]} />\n\nBanner copy is passed via the default slot. Inline markdown (`**bold**`, links) is supported when rendering from the content collection.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n- Renders as `<a>` when `href` is set, otherwise `<div>`. A trailing arrow icon is appended in link mode.\n- The dismiss button is absolutely positioned on the right when `dismissible` is true.\n\n### Scroll behavior\n\n- On page load, the banner's natural height is measured and set explicitly so CSS height transitions can run.\n- **Scroll down** (delta > 5px): banner collapses to `height: 0`.\n- **Scroll up** (delta < -5px): banner expands back to its natural height.\n- **Dismiss**: sets `height: 0`, stores `\"announcement-dismissed\"` in `sessionStorage`, then `display: none` after the transition ends. Focus moves to the first focusable element in `[data-nav-bar]`.\n\n### A11y\n\n- `role=\"status\"` and `aria-label=\"Site announcement\"` on the wrapper.\n- Close button has `aria-label=\"Dismiss announcement\"`.\n- Arrow icon is `aria-hidden=\"true\"`.\n\n## Data source: the `announcements` content collection\n\nBanners are **not** hardcoded — they're markdown files in `src/content/announcements/`. The layout reads the collection at build time, picks the currently-active entry, and renders it. Empty directory → no banner.\n\n### Schema (`src/content.config.ts`)\n\n```ts\nconst announcements = defineCollection({\n  loader: glob({ pattern: \"**/*.md\", base: \"./src/content/announcements\" }),\n  schema: z.object({\n    href: z.string().optional(),\n    dismissible: z.boolean().default(true),\n    startsAt: z.coerce.date().optional(),\n    endsAt: z.coerce.date().optional(),\n    enabled: z.boolean().default(true),\n    priority: z.number().default(0),\n  }),\n});\n```\n\n### Frontmatter fields\n\n| Field         | Type      | Default | Purpose                                                                   |\n|---------------|-----------|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| `href`        | `string?` | —       | Makes the banner a link                                                   |\n| `dismissible` | `boolean` | `true`  | Passed through to the component's dismiss button                          |\n| `startsAt`    | `Date?`   | —       | Banner is hidden before this date (UTC, ISO format)                       |\n| `endsAt`      | `Date?`   | —       | Banner auto-expires after this date                                       |\n| `enabled`     | `boolean` | `true`  | Manual on/off — useful to stage content without deleting                  |\n| `priority`    | `number`  | `0`     | Tie-breaker when multiple entries are active; highest wins                |\n\n### Selection logic (in Layout.astro)\n\n1. Load all entries via `getCollection(\"announcements\")`.\n2. Keep only entries where `enabled === true`.\n3. Keep only entries whose `startsAt` is in the past (or missing).\n4. Keep only entries whose `endsAt` is in the future (or missing).\n5. Sort by `priority` desc, then `startsAt` desc.\n6. Take the first; if nothing remains, no banner is rendered.\n\n## Usage patterns\n\n### Publish a banner now\n\nCreate `src/content/announcements/launch.md`:\n\n```md\n---\nhref: \"/launch\"\ndismissible: true\nenabled: true\n---\n\n**Launching today:** our new dashboard\n```\n\nCommit and deploy. Banner appears immediately.\n\n### Schedule a banner for later\n\n```md\n---\nhref: \"/series-a\"\nstartsAt: \"2026-05-01\"\nendsAt: \"2026-05-15\"\nenabled: true\n---\n\n**New:** Announcing our Series A\n```\n\nHidden before May 1, 2026. Auto-expires after May 15.\n\n### Temporarily hide without deleting\n\n```md\n---\nenabled: false\n---\n\nContent stays here for when you want it back.\n```\n\n## Build-time gotcha\n\nFiltering uses `new Date()` evaluated **at build time**, not in the browser. If `endsAt` passes between deploys, the banner is still shown until the next rebuild.\n\nCommon mitigations:\n\n- **Scheduled rebuilds** — Netlify, Vercel, and Cloudflare Pages all support cron-triggered deploys. Nightly is usually enough.\n- **Client-side expiry check** — add a small script that hides the banner if `endsAt < now`. The data is in the DOM at build time; JS just re-validates.\n\nFor most marketing sites, nightly rebuilds are fine. Add the client-side check if you publish time-sensitive banners (\"sale ends at midnight\").\n\n## Notes\n\n- Dismissal uses `sessionStorage`, so it resets per session (not persistent).\n- Designed to be rendered into `Nav.astro`'s `announcement` slot — that's where it sits inside the grid layout.\n- The component itself knows nothing about collections — it just receives slot content and props. That keeps it reusable for any data source (JSON, CMS, env var, etc.).",
