	"import Preview from \"@components/_docs/Preview.astro\";\nimport Button from \"@components/Button.astro\";\nimport ButtonGroup from \"@components/ButtonGroup.astro\";\n\nA pure layout primitive — no logic, no scripts. Children render in a `flex flex-wrap` row with consistent gap, falling onto a new line on narrow viewports.\n\n## Preview\n\n<Preview label=\"Two buttons\">\n  <ButtonGroup>\n    <Button label=\"Learn more\" href=\"#features\" />\n    <Button label=\"Get a demo\" variant=\"secondary\" href=\"/demo\" />\n  </ButtonGroup>\n</Preview>\n\n<Preview label=\"Wraps on narrow viewports\">\n  <ButtonGroup>\n    <Button label=\"Primary\" />\n    <Button label=\"Secondary\" variant=\"secondary\" />\n    <Button label=\"Tertiary\" variant=\"tertiary\" />\n    <Button label=\"Read docs\" href=\"/docs\" variant=\"secondary\" />\n  </ButtonGroup>\n</Preview>\n\n## Props\n\nNone — children are passed via the default `<slot />`.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n- `flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4` on the wrapper. Children inherit the gap; rows wrap on overflow.\n- The `mt-4` is baked in — the component assumes the group sits below a heading or paragraph.\n\n## Usage\n\n```astro\n---\nimport ButtonGroup from \"@components/ButtonGroup.astro\";\nimport Button from \"@components/Button.astro\";\n---\n\n<ButtonGroup>\n  <Button label=\"Learn more\" href=\"#features\" />\n  <Button label=\"Get a demo\" variant=\"secondary\" href=\"/demo\" />\n</ButtonGroup>\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The baked-in `mt-4` margin assumes the group sits below text. If you need it flush against a sibling (e.g. inside a card), wrap with `class=\"!mt-0\"` or similar.\n- Anything goes inside — not just `Button`. Mix in `<a>`, `<Clickable>`, badges, etc. as long as flex-row layout makes sense.",
	"src/content/components/button-group.mdx",
