	[166],
	"CopyButton",
	"import Preview from \"@components/_docs/Preview.astro\";\nimport PropsTable from \"@components/_docs/PropsTable.astro\";\nimport CodeBlock from \"@components/CodeBlock.astro\";\n\nA pragmatic code block primitive for docs and marketing pages. Built on top of Astro's built-in `<Code />` component (so syntax highlighting is server-rendered shiki — zero client JS for highlighting), with a small client script for the copy button.\n\n## Preview\n\n<Preview label=\"Default\" align=\"stretch\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-2xl\">\n    <CodeBlock\n      lang=\"ts\"\n      title=\"example.ts\"\n      code={`function greet(name: string) {\\n  return \\`Hello, \\${name}!\\`;\\n}\\n\\nconsole.log(greet(\"world\"));`}\n    />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n<Preview label=\"With line numbers and highlight\" align=\"stretch\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-2xl\">\n    <CodeBlock\n      lang=\"js\"\n      title=\"config.js\"\n      showLineNumbers\n      highlight={[3, 4]}\n      code={`export default {\\n  name: \"starter\",\\n  version: \"1.0.0\",\\n  features: [\"tooltip\", \"code-block\"],\\n};`}\n    />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n<Preview label=\"Minimal — no toolbar\" align=\"stretch\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-2xl\">\n    <CodeBlock\n      lang=\"bash\"\n      hideLang\n      hideCopy\n      code={`npm install\\nnpm run dev`}\n    />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n## Props\n\n<PropsTable props={[\n  { name: \"code\", type: \"string\", required: true, description: \"Source code to render and highlight.\" },\n  { name: \"lang\", type: \"string\", default: '\"plaintext\"', description: \"Shiki language id (e.g. \\\"ts\\\", \\\"jsx\\\", \\\"bash\\\").\" },\n  { name: \"title\", type: \"string\", description: \"Filename or label shown in the title bar.\" },\n  { name: \"highlight\", type: \"number[]\", default: \"[]\", description: \"1-based line numbers to highlight.\" },\n  { name: \"showLineNumbers\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\", description: \"Show a 1-based line-number gutter (CSS counter).\" },\n  { name: \"hideLang\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\", description: \"Hide the language badge in the toolbar.\" },\n  { name: \"hideCopy\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\", description: \"Hide the copy button in the toolbar.\" },\n  { name: \"class\", type: \"string\", description: \"Additional classes on the figure element.\" },\n]} />\n\n## Mechanism\n\n- **Highlighting** — Astro's `<Code />` runs shiki at build/SSR time. No client-side highlighter is shipped to the browser.\n- **Line highlight** — implemented as a one-line shiki transformer (`name: \"codeblock-highlight\"`) that adds `data-line-highlight=\"true\"` to matching `<span class=\"line\">` rows. CSS draws the highlight band.\n- **Line numbers** — pure CSS counter on `.line` elements. No per-line markup needed.\n- **Copy button** — the `CopyButton` component reads the literal `code` string from the prop, so what gets copied is exactly what was rendered (no whitespace surprises from copying DOM text).\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `<Code />` component must be imported from `astro:components` — that's the project rule (see `feedback_astro_shiki_cloudflare.md`). Don't shell out to `shiki.codeToHtml` directly; static HTML truncates on Cloudflare builds.\n- Shiki appends a trailing empty line to its output. The CSS rule `.line:last-child:empty::before { content: \"\"; }` suppresses the number for that ghost line.\n- For inline code, use the standard markdown `` `like this` `` — this component is for block-level snippets only.",
	"src/content/components/code-block.mdx",
