	"Labeled form input row. Wraps text/email/password/url/tel/number/search/textarea/select/checkbox/radio with label, helper, and inline error region — ARIA wired automatically.",
	11,
	"src/components/Field.astro",
	[191],
	"import Preview from \"@components/_docs/Preview.astro\";\nimport PropsTable from \"@components/_docs/PropsTable.astro\";\nimport Field from \"@components/Field.astro\";\n\nA single-input row that handles the boring-but-easy-to-get-wrong parts of form fields: associating a `<label>` to its input, wiring `aria-describedby` to helper and error text, surfacing `aria-invalid` for invalid state, and reserving space so the form doesn't jump when an error appears.\n\nDesigned to be paired with `Form`, which surfaces native validation messages into each Field's error region automatically. Works standalone too.\n\n## Preview\n\n<Preview label=\"Text + email + textarea + select + checkbox\" align=\"stretch\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-md space-y-2\">\n    <Field label=\"Full name\" name=\"name\" placeholder=\"Jane Doe\" required helper=\"As it appears on your ID.\" />\n    <Field label=\"Email\" name=\"email\" type=\"email\" placeholder=\"jane@example.com\" required />\n    <Field label=\"Message\" name=\"message\" type=\"textarea\" rows={3} />\n    <Field label=\"Plan\" name=\"plan\" type=\"select\" options={[\n      { value: \"free\", label: \"Free\" },\n      { value: \"pro\", label: \"Pro\" },\n      { value: \"team\", label: \"Team\" },\n    ]} />\n    <Field label=\"Subscribe to newsletter\" name=\"newsletter\" type=\"checkbox\" />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n<Preview label=\"Pre-set error state\" align=\"stretch\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-md\">\n    <Field label=\"Email\" name=\"email\" type=\"email\" value=\"not-an-email\" error=\"Please enter a valid email address.\" />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n## Props\n\n<PropsTable props={[\n  { name: \"label\", type: \"string\", required: true, description: \"Visible label text.\" },\n  { name: \"name\", type: \"string\", required: true, description: \"Form data key.\" },\n  { name: \"type\", type: '\"text\" | \"email\" | \"password\" | \"url\" | \"tel\" | \"number\" | \"search\" | \"textarea\" | \"select\" | \"checkbox\" | \"radio\"', default: '\"text\"', description: \"Input type.\" },\n  { name: \"id\", type: \"string\", description: \"Stable ID. Auto-generated if omitted.\" },\n  { name: \"value\", type: \"string | number\", description: \"Initial value.\" },\n  { name: \"placeholder\", type: \"string\", description: \"Placeholder text (text-like inputs).\" },\n  { name: \"helper\", type: \"string\", description: \"Helper text shown under the input.\" },\n  { name: \"error\", type: \"string\", description: \"Pre-set error message. Live validation overrides this.\" },\n  { name: \"required\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\" },\n  { name: \"disabled\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\" },\n  { name: \"readonly\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\" },\n  { name: \"autocomplete\", type: \"string\", description: 'Native autocomplete hint, e.g. \"email\", \"name\", \"off\".' },\n  { name: \"pattern\", type: \"string\", description: \"Pattern attribute for text inputs.\" },\n  { name: \"minlength / maxlength\", type: \"number\", description: \"String length bounds.\" },\n  { name: \"min / max / step\", type: \"string | number\", description: \"Number / date input bounds.\" },\n  { name: \"rows\", type: \"number\", default: \"4\", description: \"Textarea row count.\" },\n  { name: \"options\", type: \"{ value: string; label: string }[]\", description: 'Select options (when type=\"select\" and no slot is provided).' },\n  { name: \"labelHidden\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\", description: \"Visually hide the label (kept for screen readers).\" },\n  { name: \"class\", type: \"string\", description: \"Additional classes on the wrapper.\" },\n]} />\n\n## Slots\n\nFor `type=\"select\"`, the default slot can be used to write your own `<option>` elements (overrides `options`):\n\n```astro\n<Field label=\"Country\" name=\"country\" type=\"select\">\n  <option value=\"\">Select country</option>\n  <option value=\"us\">United States</option>\n  <option value=\"uk\">United Kingdom</option>\n</Field>\n```\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- `<label for=\"…\">` matched to input id.\n- `aria-describedby` points at helper text, error text, or both.\n- `aria-invalid=\"true\"` set whenever an error is present (either from the `error` prop or from live validation).\n- Required fields show a red `*` next to the label (decorative — `aria-hidden`); the actual signal to screen readers is the input's `required` attribute.\n- The error region uses `aria-live=\"polite\"` so changes are announced without interrupting.\n- The error region reserves `min-height: 1em` so the form doesn't jump when an error message appears.\n- For `checkbox` / `radio`, label and input are wrapped together in a single `<label>` so clicking either toggles the input.\n\n## Working with Form\n\nWhen wrapped in `Form`, validation messages flow automatically:\n\n```astro\n<Form action=\"/api/contact\" method=\"POST\">\n  <Field label=\"Email\" name=\"email\" type=\"email\" required />\n  <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n</Form>\n```\n\nIf the user submits with an invalid email, the Field's error region populates with the browser's native `validationMessage`, focus jumps to the first invalid input, and `aria-invalid` is set. As the user fixes the input, the error clears.\n\nOutside a Form, the `error` prop is the only error path — set it from your own validation logic.\n\n## Notes\n\n- For radio groups, render multiple Field components with the same `name` and different `value` props.\n- For file uploads, currently bypass Field and use a plain `<input type=\"file\">` — file inputs have unique label/styling needs that didn't fit cleanly. May get its own component later.\n- The `sr-only` class is provided by Tailwind v4 — `labelHidden` relies on it.",
	"src/content/components/field.mdx",
