	"import Preview from \"@components/_docs/Preview.astro\";\nimport { Image, Picture } from \"astro:assets\";\nimport demo from \"@images/feature-1.webp\";\n\n`<Image>` and `<Picture>` are Astro's built-in image components (from `astro:assets`). They run the source through **Sharp at build time** — resizing, transcoding, and emitting hashed files into `dist/_astro/*` — then output an `<img>`/`<picture>` with intrinsic `width`/`height` so the layout never shifts (CLS). This is the **standard** for every content/decorative image in the starter; raw `<img>` is reserved for `/public` assets (SVG logos, favicons) and runtime/CMS URL strings.\n\n> **Works on Cloudflare with no adapter.** The starter is pure-static (`output: 'static'`, no adapter), so Sharp runs during `npm run build` and Cloudflare just serves the static `/_astro/*` output. Do **not** add `@astrojs/cloudflare` for images — its image service is a passthrough that ships unoptimized/broken AVIF.\n\n## Preview\n\n<Preview label=\"<Image> — single optimized source\" align=\"start\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-md\">\n    <Image src={demo} alt=\"Schema builder screenshot\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"w-full h-auto\" />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n<Preview label=\"<Picture> — multi-format (AVIF → WebP), responsive widths\" align=\"start\">\n  <div class=\"w-full max-w-md\">\n    <Picture\n      src={demo}\n      alt=\"Schema builder screenshot\"\n      widths={[400, 800]}\n      sizes=\"(min-width: 768px) 400px, 100vw\"\n      formats={[\"avif\", \"webp\"]}\n      fallbackFormat=\"webp\"\n      quality={70}\n      loading=\"lazy\"\n      decoding=\"async\"\n      class=\"w-full h-auto\"\n    />\n  </div>\n</Preview>\n\n## Usage\n\n```astro\n---\nimport { Image, Picture } from \"astro:assets\";\n// Import the asset — this is what unlocks optimization + dimension inference.\nimport hero from \"@images/hero.webp\";\nimport shot from \"@images/screenshot.webp\";\n---\n\n{/* Single optimized image. width/height inferred from the import. */}\n<Image src={shot} alt=\"Schema builder\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n\n{/* Above-the-fold / LCP image — never lazy-load it. */}\n<Image src={hero} alt=\"\" widths={[800, 1600]} sizes=\"100vw\"\n       loading=\"eager\" fetchpriority=\"high\" />\n\n{/* Multi-format + responsive: emits <picture> with AVIF then WebP. */}\n<Picture\n  src={hero}\n  alt=\"Product hero\"\n  widths={[600, 1200, 1800]}\n  sizes=\"(min-width: 1024px) 1100px, 100vw\"\n  formats={[\"avif\", \"webp\"]}\n  fallbackFormat=\"webp\"\n  quality={70}\n/>\n```\n\n## `<Image>` vs `<Picture>`\n\n| Use | When |\n|---|---|\n| **`<Image>`** | The default. One source, one output format. Add `widths` + `sizes` for a responsive `srcset`. |\n| **`<Picture>`** | You want **multiple formats** (AVIF with a WebP fallback) or art-direction. Emits a `<picture>` with `<source>` per format. Best for large hero/banner images where AVIF's extra savings matter. |\n\n## Rules (the ones that actually bite)\n\n- **Pass the imported asset, not its `.src`.** `src={img}` ✅ — `src={img.src}` ❌. The string form is just a URL and silently skips optimization *and* the `width`/`height` inference that prevents CLS.\n- **Import from `src/images/`** (aliased `@images/*`). Only un-optimizable assets (SVGs, favicons, OG/social images) belong in `public/` and stay as raw `<img>`.\n- **Don't lazy-load the LCP image.** The hero / first above-the-fold image gets `loading=\"eager\"` + `fetchpriority=\"high\"`. Everything below the fold gets `loading=\"lazy\"` + `decoding=\"async\"`. Lazy-loading the LCP element directly tanks the LCP metric.\n- **`alt` is required.** Use a real description for meaningful images, `alt=\"\"` (+ `aria-hidden=\"true\"`) for decorative ones.\n- **The same imported asset is deduped.** Reusing one import across a page emits a single `/_astro/*` file referenced everywhere.\n\n## Accepting images in your own components\n\nWhen a component renders an image it owns, type the prop as **`ImageMetadata`** and render `<Image>`:\n\n```astro\n---\nimport type { ImageMetadata } from \"astro\";\nimport { Image } from \"astro:assets\";\n\ninterface Props {\n  src: ImageMetadata;   // an imported asset, not a string\n  alt: string;\n}\nconst { src, alt } = Astro.props;\n---\n<Image src={src} alt={alt} loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n```\n\nFor primitives that must also accept **runtime/CMS URL strings** (`Avatar`, `Media`, `SliderBasicMap`), the starter pattern is a union prop that branches on the type — imported assets get optimized, strings fall through to a plain `<img>`:\n\n```astro\n---\nimport type { ImageMetadata } from \"astro\";\nimport { Image } from \"astro:assets\";\n\ninterface Props {\n  src?: string | ImageMetadata;\n  alt: string;\n}\nconst { src, alt } = Astro.props;\n---\n{src && (typeof src === \"string\"\n  ? <img src={src} alt={alt} loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n  : <Image src={src} alt={alt} loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />)}\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Content-collection images** go through `astro:assets` too: use `image()` in the Zod schema (`heroImage: image().optional()`) so frontmatter image paths resolve to `ImageMetadata` and optimize on build.\n- **Remote images** (a literal URL string to `<Image>`) require explicit `width`/`height` and need the domain allow-listed in `image.domains`/`image.remotePatterns`; they aren't downloaded and re-encoded the way local imports are.\n- **`quality`** accepts a number (`0–100`) or a preset (`\"low\" | \"mid\" | \"high\" | \"max\"`). 70 is a good default for photographic content.\n- **SVGs** don't benefit from Sharp — keep them as inline `<svg>`, an `astro-icon` `<Icon>`, or a `/public` `<img>`.",
