	"PageTransition",
	"SmoothScroll",
	"import PropsTable from \"@components/_docs/PropsTable.astro\";\n\nThe base HTML layout wrapper for every page. Sets up `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>`, loads global styles and fonts, includes the navigation, and optionally injects Google Analytics via Partytown.\n\n## Props\n\n<PropsTable props={[\n  { name: \"title\", type: \"string\", default: '\"Astro Playground\"', description: \"Page <title> tag.\" },\n  { name: \"theme\", type: '\"light\" | \"dark\" | \"brand\"', default: '\"light\"', description: \"Sets the `data-theme` attribute on `<html>`. Flips every CSS token (canvas, fg, stroke, etc.) for the whole page — including the nav and announcement bar.\" },\n  { name: \"skipLoader\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\", description: \"Omit the intro Loader overlay on this page.\" },\n  { name: \"hideFooter\", type: \"boolean\", default: \"false\", description: \"Omit the site copyright footer on this page.\" },\n]} />\n\n## Mechanism\n\n### `<head>`\n\n- Imports the Archivo Variable font via `@fontsource-variable/archivo`.\n- Imports `global.css` (all theme tokens, utilities, and base styles).\n- Sets charset, viewport, favicon, and generator meta tags.\n\n### Google Analytics (optional)\n\n- Reads `PUBLIC_GTAG_ID` from environment variables.\n- If set, loads the gtag script with `type=\"text/partytown\"` — this offloads the analytics script to a web worker via `@astrojs/partytown`, keeping the main thread clean.\n- If not set, no tracking code runs at all.\n\n### `<body>`\n\n- Boots `<SmoothScroll />` (Locomotive Scroll v5 / Lenis) on every page, then the intro `<Loader />` (unless `skipLoader`), then `<Nav />`.\n- Includes a **skip-to-content** link (`<a href=\"#main\">`) — visually hidden by default, becomes visible on focus for keyboard users.\n- Page content is injected via `<slot />`.\n- Renders `<Footer />` after the slot unless `hideFooter` is set.\n- Ends with `<PageTransition />` — a covering fade overlay between same-origin navigations, not a client router.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Astro page\n\n```astro\n---\nimport Layout from \"../layouts/Layout.astro\";\n---\n\n<Layout title=\"Features\">\n  <main id=\"main\">\n    {/* page content */}\n  </main>\n</Layout>\n```\n\n### Astro page with dark theme\n\nPass `theme=\"dark\"` as a prop. The attribute lands on `<html>`, so every component on the page — including the nav, announcement bar, and any `SectionMain` — picks up dark tokens automatically.\n\n```astro\n---\nimport Layout from \"../layouts/Layout.astro\";\n---\n\n<Layout title=\"Manifesto\" theme=\"dark\">\n  <main id=\"main\">\n    {/* renders against the dark token set */}\n  </main>\n</Layout>\n```\n\n### MDX page\n\n`.mdx` files in `src/pages/` can use `Layout` directly via the `layout:` frontmatter key. All other frontmatter keys are forwarded as props — including `title` and `theme`.\n\n```mdx\n---\nlayout: ../layouts/Layout.astro\ntitle: Brand\ntheme: dark\n---\n\nimport Grainient from \"@components/Grainient.astro\";\n\n# Brand\n\nThe whole page is dark — no per-section overrides needed.\n\n<div class=\"relative h-[50vh]\">\n  <Grainient />\n</div>\n```\n\nThe same works for any `.md`/`.mdx` page — blog posts, changelog entries, marketing one-offs.\n\n### Per-section theme island\n\nIf most of the page is light but one section needs to flip (e.g. a dark \"pricing\" band on a light landing page), don't change the layout — set `data-theme` on a wrapper around just that section. The token cascade handles the rest:\n\n```astro\n<Layout title=\"Pricing\">\n  <main id=\"main\">\n    {/* light by default */}\n    <SectionMain padding=\"lg\">…</SectionMain>\n\n    {/* dark island */}\n    <div data-theme=\"dark\">\n      <SectionMain padding=\"lg\">\n        {/* fg / canvas / stroke all swap inside this wrapper */}\n      </SectionMain>\n    </div>\n\n    {/* back to light */}\n    <SectionMain padding=\"lg\">…</SectionMain>\n  </main>\n</Layout>\n```\n\nValid theme values are `light`, `dark`, and `brand` — see `src/styles/global.css` for the token definitions of each.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The skip link targets `#main` — pages should include `id=\"main\"` on their `<main>` element.\n- The skip link sits **after** `<Nav />` in the DOM, so it appears after the nav in tab order. Intentional — the nav's own skip logic handles initial focus.\n- Google Analytics only loads when `PUBLIC_GTAG_ID` is set in `.env`.\n- `theme` is read from either `Astro.props.theme` (Astro pages) or `Astro.props.frontmatter.theme` (MDX/Markdown pages with `layout:`), so the same prop works in both contexts.",
