	"LogoMarquee",
	"Infinitely scrolling row of logos with a centered \"Trusted by\" label, pure CSS animation.",
	"src/components/LogoMarquee.astro",
	[93],
	"import Preview from \"@components/_docs/Preview.astro\";\nimport PropsTable from \"@components/_docs/PropsTable.astro\";\nimport LogoMarquee from \"@components/LogoMarquee.astro\";\nimport { Icon } from \"astro-icon/components\";\n\nA continuous, JS-free marquee. The slot is rendered twice — when the first set scrolls out, the duplicate is already in place, so the loop is seamless.\n\n## Preview\n\n<Preview label=\"Lucide-icon marquee\">\n  <LogoMarquee class=\"border-y border-stroke py-8 w-full\">\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:figma\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:github\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:slack\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:linkedin\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:youtube\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:twitch\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:dribbble\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n    <Icon name=\"lucide:codepen\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0 text-fg-muted\" />\n  </LogoMarquee>\n</Preview>\n\n## Props\n\n<PropsTable props={[\n  { name: \"class\", type: \"string\", default: '\"\"', description: \"Extra classes on the overflow container — typically borders and vertical padding.\" },\n]} />\n\nChildren are passed via the default `<slot />`.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n- Outer container has `overflow-hidden` to clip content at the viewport edges.\n- A flex inner container uses the `animate-marquee` utility (defined in `global.css`) — `translateX(0)` to `translateX(-50%)` over 30 seconds.\n- The `<slot />` is rendered **twice**. When the first set translates out of view, the duplicate has scrolled in to replace it — no visible seam.\n- A \"Trusted by leading data companies\" label is absolutely positioned above the marquee with a `bg-canvas` background to punch through the border.\n\n## Usage\n\n```astro\n---\nimport LogoMarquee from \"@components/LogoMarquee.astro\";\n---\n\n<LogoMarquee class=\"border-t border-stroke py-6\">\n  <img src=\"/logos/company-1.svg\" alt=\"Company 1\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0\" />\n  <img src=\"/logos/company-2.svg\" alt=\"Company 2\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0\" />\n  <img src=\"/logos/company-3.svg\" alt=\"Company 3\" class=\"h-6 w-auto shrink-0\" />\n</LogoMarquee>\n```\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- You need enough children to fill the container width — otherwise the seam between the two duplicate sets is visible as a gap.\n- The slot is duplicated in HTML, so each child appears in the DOM twice. Avoid putting interactive elements inside (clickable logos will have two activations registering against analytics, etc.).\n- The animation is pure CSS. Speed comes from the `marquee` keyframes in `global.css` (currently 30s linear).\n- The \"Trusted by\" label assumes the page background matches `--color-canvas` so its `bg-canvas` punches through any overlapping border cleanly.",
